          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Monty Hall Problem",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ],
              "colour": "#8b5cc7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " On a game show there are three closed doors: one hides a car and the other two hide goats. The car is equally likely to be behind each door. You pick one door (call it Door 1). The host knows where the car is and ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "always",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " opens one of the two remaining doors to reveal a goat.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p35-q37-narrative2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If both remaining doors hide goats, the host chooses uniformly at random which one to open. After opening a goat door (say Door 3), the host offers you the choice to ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "stay",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " with Door 1 or ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "switch",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " to the other unopened door (Door 2).",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p35-q37-definition-intro",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Let the events be",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p35-q37-event-definitions",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "center",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\begin{aligned}C_i&=\\text{car is behind Door }i\\\\H_j&=\\text{host opens Door }j\\\\W_S&=\\text{win if switch}\\\\W_T&=\\text{win if stay.}\\end{aligned}",
              "display": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p35-q37-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p35-q37-a-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Find ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "P(C_1),\\ P(C_2),\\ P(C_3)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(C_1)=P(C_2)=P(C_3)=\\dfrac13$.",
          "worked": "Each of the three car locations is equally likely.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(C_1)=P(C_2)=P(C_3)&=\\frac13.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q37-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p35-q37-b-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Find ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "P(H_3\\mid C_1),\\ P(H_3\\mid C_2)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", and ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "P(H_3\\mid C_3)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " from the host’s stated behaviour.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(H_3\\mid C_1)=\\dfrac12$, $P(H_3\\mid C_2)=1$, $P(H_3\\mid C_3)=0$.",
          "worked": "If the car is behind Door 1, the host chooses equally between Doors 2 and 3. If it is behind Door 2, the host must open Door 3. If it is behind Door 3, the host cannot open Door 3.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(H_3\\mid C_1)&=\\frac12,\\\\P(H_3\\mid C_2)&=1,\\\\P(H_3\\mid C_3)&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q37-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p35-q37-c-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Find ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "P(C_1\\mid H_3)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "P(C_2\\mid H_3)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p35-q37-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "P(C_1\\mid H_3)=\\frac13,\\qquad P(C_2\\mid H_3)=\\frac23.",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p35-q37-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Sum the three car-location cases to obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "P(H_3)=\\frac12",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then apply the conditional probability formula.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The three car-location cases are mutually exclusive and exhaustive.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(H_3)&=P(C_1)P(H_3\\mid C_1)+P(C_2)P(H_3\\mid C_2)+P(C_3)P(H_3\\mid C_3)\\\\P(H_3)&=\\frac13\\times\\frac12+\\frac13\\times1+\\frac13\\times0\\\\P(H_3)&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(C_1\\mid H_3)&=\\frac{P(C_1\\cap H_3)}{P(H_3)}\\\\P(C_1\\mid H_3)&=\\frac{\\frac13\\times\\frac12}{\\frac12}\\\\P(C_1\\mid H_3)&=\\frac13,\\\\P(C_2\\mid H_3)&=\\frac{P(C_2\\cap H_3)}{P(H_3)}\\\\P(C_2\\mid H_3)&=\\frac{\\frac13\\times1}{\\frac12}\\\\P(C_2\\mid H_3)&=\\frac23.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 96
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q37-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p35-q37-d-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Hence, find ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "P(W_T\\mid H_3)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "P(W_S\\mid H_3)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and decide which action (stay or switch) maximises your chance of winning given that the host opened Door 3.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
