        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p35-q37-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "P(W_T\\mid H_3)=\\frac13,\\qquad P(W_S\\mid H_3)=\\frac23.",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Switch.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p35-q37-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Staying wins when the car is behind Door 1; switching wins when it is behind Door 2.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Given that Door 3 has been opened, staying wins exactly when the car is behind Door 1, and switching wins exactly when it is behind Door 2.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(W_T\\mid H_3)&=P(C_1\\mid H_3)\\\\P(W_T\\mid H_3)&=\\frac13,\\\\P(W_S\\mid H_3)&=P(C_2\\mid H_3)\\\\P(W_S\\mid H_3)&=\\frac23.\\end{align*}$$\nSwitch, since $\\dfrac23>\\dfrac13$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
